From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] gdikmt, d3d9umd, d3d10umd: residency for WDDM 2.0 kernel drivers

With a WDDM 2.0 kernel driver Windows no longer makes allocations resident
for the user-mode driver: a command buffer naming one that wasn't made
resident is dropped ("Allocation is not requested to be resident"), and
from D3DKMT the whole device is put in error.

- gdikmt_wddm2_make_resident (D3D9 and D3D10/11 drivers): a paging queue
  made on first use, MakeResident after every allocation created or opened,
  then a wait for the paging fence. The runtimes' pfnMakeResidentCb reports
  pending paging work as E_PENDING (not STATUS_PENDING), so the wait happens
  whenever a paging fence value comes back; a command buffer sent before
  the paging work is done is dropped ("allocation has not been fully
  committed").
- The OpenGL D3DKMT path does the same after D3DKMTCreateAllocation and
  D3DKMTOpenResource (the window's back buffer is a resource shared from
  another device, resident only for that one).
- d3d9umd declares the WDDM 2.0 interface when the kernel driver is WDDM 2.0
  (VIOGPU_ADAPTERINFO::Flags.Wddm2), so the runtime hands it the residency
  callbacks; WDDM 1.x kernel drivers have no paging queue and nothing
  changes.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gdikmt/gdikmt.h
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #ifndef gdikmt_h
 #define gdikmt_h
 
+#include <stdbool.h>
 #include <windows.h>
 #include <winternl.h>
 #include <d3dkmthk.h>
@@ -100,6 +101,17 @@
 extern "C" {
 #endif
 
+/* WDDM 2.0 residency for the D3D user-mode drivers (gdikmt_wddm2.c): their paging queue, made on first use */
+struct gdikmt_wddm2_residency {
+   D3DKMT_HANDLE hPagingQueue;
+   D3DKMT_HANDLE hPagingFence;
+   bool tried;
+};
+struct _D3DDDI_DEVICECALLBACKS;
+void
+gdikmt_wddm2_make_resident(struct gdikmt_wddm2_residency *residency, const struct _D3DDDI_DEVICECALLBACKS *cb,
+                           HANDLE hRTDevice, const D3DKMT_HANDLE *handles, UINT count);
+
 struct gdikmt_device *gdikmt_create_from_hdc(HDC hDC);
 /* Opens the adapter with this LUID through the D3DKMT* functions */
 struct gdikmt_device *gdikmt_create_from_luid(LUID luid);
